course: dictionary
lesson: 13969
title: Liquefy and changing states
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To liquefy something is to turn it into a liquid. Liquid is the state of matter that flows and takes the shape of its container, like water. The ending -fy means make or turn into, so liquefy means make into a liquid.
explain: Liquefy can also mean making a solid or a gas become a liquid. «The ice liquefies when the sun warms it.» The clue is warm and melting: heat turns the solid ice into water. «Gas can be liquefied by cooling and squeezing it.» Here the clues are cooling and squeezing, which turn a gas into a liquid.
explain: Liquefy is a science word, but you can meet it in the kitchen too. «The blender will liquefy the strawberries into a smooth drink.» When you meet liquefy, ask: what goes in, and what comes out? If the answer is a liquid, you have found its meaning.
fact: Liquefy means to turn into a liquid, or to make a solid or gas become a liquid.
fact: Things can liquefy when they are heated, cooled or squeezed.
fact: «Liquid nitrogen» is nitrogen that has been cooled until it has become a liquid.
fact: «LPG» is a gas that is squeezed into a liquid, so it can be stored in a small tank for a barbecue.
fact: Earthquakes can liquefy wet soil, so the ground moves and flows like a liquid.
exercise: «The ice liquefies when it melts.» What does liquefies mean here? | *Turns into a liquid | Becomes hard as a rock | Breaks into tiny pieces | Turns into a gas that floats away
exercise: «The blender will liquefy the fruit.» What happens to the fruit? | It gets bigger | *It turns into a smooth liquid | It freezes into a solid | It is cut into small chunks only
exercise: Which of these is a way to liquefy a gas? | Cover it with a blanket | Make it hotter and let it float away | *Cool it and squeeze it | Shake it gently
test: «Earthquakes can liquefy wet soil.» What can happen to the soil? | *It turns runny and flows like a liquid | It floats up into the sky | It changes colour only | It becomes hard as stone
test: Jayden asks, «What does liquefy mean?» Which answer is correct? | To cut something into pieces | *To turn something into a liquid | To make something lighter | To freeze something solid
exam: Which sentence uses liquefy correctly? | *The sun liquefied the ice cube on the plate | The ice cube liquefied my brother | She liquefied her homework and handed it in | The dog liquefied its bone in the garden
